  "body": "I have been experimenting with kokoro-js for a while now, I am building an app that streams large unknown texts on-device. It all seems to boil down to proper chunking.  The sweet spot for my tests seems to be at chunks of around 160 characters. The issue I have with this is some sentences sound weird when you chunk them, because of the very noticeable pause between two chunks, while logically its one sentence. I have improved my chunking algo to attempt to chunk at \"natural\" places, like comma, colon, semicolon, etc. And it helps, but still the above problem persists. Have you guys solved this? If yes, how did you do it?",
